# L §3.6 example (2.1-C7b-18): `rule inherited beats community, moved`, so "an inheritance paid from savings goes to the
# heir" ("The example labels an inheritance the heir's, money moved from another savings account as it was").  As
# L3_6_parts_walk, but spend2 is an inheritance of 400.00 from konto to konto2 with heir ania: both `inherited` and
# `moved` apply, and `inherited` wins, so konto2 holds Ania's 400.00 beside the couple's 600.00 that mv moved (figures
# carried through), and nothing of Tomek's though the take reached his part.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key persons
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by civ_arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w v civ order (if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1) prorata ties by (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1)
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
input inh_day: date
input inh_amt: money PLN
input spend_day: date
input spend_amt: money PLN
input mv_day: date
input mv_amt: money PLN
input spend2_day: date
input spend2_amt: money PLN

def civ_arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = (if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0)
  rule inherited beats community, moved = (if p == m.heir then 1 else 0) when m in inheritances
  rule moved beats community = m.cash.amount of p / m.cash.amount when m in transfers and m.cash.from in savings

move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
move inh: inheritances
  on inh_day
  attr heir = tomek
  leg cash from world to konto amount inh_amt
move spend: transfers
  on spend_day
  leg cash from konto to shop amount spend_amt
move mv: transfers
  on mv_day
  leg cash from konto to konto2 amount mv_amt
move spend2: inheritances
  on spend2_day
  attr heir = ania
  leg cash from konto to konto2 amount spend2_amt

ask q: bal(konto2, 2026-06-30) of ania, bal(konto2, 2026-06-30) of tomek, bal(konto2, 2026-06-30) of ania_tomek

version civ
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 1 000.00 PLN
  inh_day = 2026-03-01
  inh_amt = 500.00 PLN
  spend_day = 2026-04-01
  spend_amt = 300.00 PLN
  mv_day = 2026-05-01
  mv_amt = 600.00 PLN
  spend2_day = 2026-06-01
  spend2_amt = 400.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (400.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 600.00 PLN)
...
